# kula decentralized ai — which server the app talks to. Expo loads, in order of priority:
#   .env.development.local   expo start / Expo Go: the Mac's local server (not in git;
#                            EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://<mac ip>:4350, key "local")
#   .env.production          a release build (npm run apk): kula's own live Supabase project
#   .env                     this file: nothing, on purpose
# Until 21.10.2026 this file carried afterhours' live project and .env.local the Mac's
# address; Expo loads .env.local in release builds too, so the apk was baked with the Mac's
# Wi-Fi address and was offline anywhere else. Never put a server here, and never use an
# .env.local: tools/release-env.mjs refuses a release build that would reach a dev server.
